{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Voices of Elohim.</b> He acknowledged that He was Elohim. And because he did not say the special Name, Moses and his companion came and said, 'from before YHWH our Elohim' — meaning, the Elohim is YHWH alone. And you will not find in all the Torah that any person mentioned it thus. And there is no objection to 'YHWH Elohim': מה תתן לי, במה אדע, אתה החלותה, אל תשחת עמך ונחלתך — for all of them are written with alef-dalet."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The argument appears to be that Pharaoh never used the phrase 'YHWH Elohim'; the cited verses, all written with the reverent alef-dalet abbreviation for the divine name, are cited as counterexamples showing that other biblical figures did pair the Name with Elohim."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:49.030660816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}